#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:122
msgid "Creating or Editing a VDI Apps"
msgstr "Creating o Editing a VDI Apps"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:124
msgid ""
"VDI Apps allow users to launch directly into commonly-used apps rather "
"than the OS desktop. Currently, VDI Apps only work with RDP Windows "
"Instances, taking advantage of native Windows Remote Application "
"functionality. Natively-hosted remote desktop applications can only be "
"presented from Windows 10 Enterprise and Education. Other versions of "
"Windows 10 can present remote applications using the procedure below:"
msgstr ""
"VDI Apps allow users to launch directly en commonly-used apps rather than "
"the OS desktop. Actualmente, VDI Apps solo work con RDP Windows Instances, "
"taking advantage of native Windows Remote Application functionality. "
"Natively-hosted remote desktop applications can solo be presented desde "
"Windows 10 Enterprise y Education. Other versions of Windows 10 can "
"present remote applications using the procedure below:"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:126
msgid "Open the Windows Registry Editor"
msgstr "Open the Windows Registry Editor"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:127
msgid ""
"Locate the following entry: "
"``HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows "
"NT\\CurrentVersion\\Terminal Server\\TSAppAllowList``"
msgstr ""
"Locate lo siguiente entry: "
"``HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Windows "
"NT\\\\CurrentVersion\\\\Terminal Server\\\\TSAppAllowList``"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:128
msgid ""
"Navigate to ``fDisabledAllowList`` and set its value to \"1\" in the "
"right-hand pane"
msgstr ""
"Navigate to ``fDisabledAllowList`` y set its value to \\\"1\\\" in the "
"right-hand pane"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:129
msgid "Add a new key under ``TSAppAllowList`` and name it \"Applications\""
msgstr "Add un nuevo key under ``TSAppAllowList`` y name it \\\"Applications\\\""

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:130
msgid "Add a new key under \"Applications\" using any name you'd like"
msgstr "Add un nuevo key under \\\"Applications\\\" using any name you'd like"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:131
msgid ""
"Within this new key, create two new string values, one called \"Name\" "
"and one called \"Path\""
msgstr ""
"Within this new key, create two new string values, one called \\\"Name\\\" "
"y one called \\\"Path\\\""

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:132
msgid ""
"The string value for \"Name\" should describe the application (ex. "
"\"Notepad\")"
msgstr ""
"The string value for \\\"Name\\\" should describe the application (ex. "
"\\\"Notepad\\\")"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:133
msgid ""
"The string value for \"Path\" should be the absolute path to the "
"executable for that application (ex. "
"\"C:\\Windows\\System32\\notepad.exe\")"
msgstr ""
"The string value for \\\"Path\\\" debería ser the absolute path to the "
"executable for that application (ex. "
"\\\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\notepad.exe\\\")"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:135
msgid ""
"VDI Apps are created by selecting :guilabel:`+ ADD` from the VDI Apps tab"
" or edit an existing one by clicking on the pencil icon from the "
"appropriate row. Configure the following, fields containing a vertical "
"blue bar along the left edge are required:"
msgstr ""
"VDI Apps are created by selecting :guilabel:`+ ADD` desde the VDI Apps tab "
"o edit un existente one by clicking on the pencil icon desde the "
"appropriate row. Configure lo siguiente, fields containing a vertical blue "
"bar along the left edge son obligatorios:"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:137
msgid "**NAME:** A friendly name for the VDI App in |morpheus|"
msgstr "**NAME:** A friendly name for the VDI App in |morpheus|"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:138
msgid "**DESCRIPTION:** A description of the virtual app type"
msgstr "**DESCRIPTION:** A description of the virtual app type"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:139
msgid ""
"**LAUNCH PREFIX:** A reference to the remote app registry prepended with "
"two pipes ( ``||`` ). For example, we might create a registry \"Chrome\" "
"for a Chrome browser VDI App and the associated launch prefix would be "
"\"||Chrome\""
msgstr ""
"**LAUNCH PREFIX:** A reference a la remote app registry prepended con two "
"pipes ( ``||`` ). Por ejemplo, we might create a registry \"Chrome\" for a "
"Chrome browser VDI App y the associated launch prefix would be "
"\"||Chrome\""

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:140
msgid ""
"**LOGO:** Upload or select a logo to represent the virtual app type to "
"users"
msgstr ""
"**LOGO:** Upload o select a logo to represent the virtual app type to "
"users"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:143
msgid "VDI Gateways"
msgstr "VDI Gateways"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:145
msgid ""
"The |morpheus| Worker is a light weight distributed worker daemon as well"
" as a scalable VDI Gateway. Currently, the features center around VDI "
"Gateway but will expand to support full plugin workloads as well as agent"
" relay capabilities."
msgstr ""
"The |morpheus| Worker is a light weight distributed worker daemon así como "
"a scalable VDI Gateway. Actualmente, the features center around VDI "
"Gateway but will expand to support full plugin workloads así como agent "
"relay capabilities."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:148
msgid "Adding VDI Gateways to |morpheus|"
msgstr "Adding VDI Gateways to |morpheus|"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:150
msgid ""
"VDI Gateways can be linked to a |morpheus| appliance and then used in VDI"
" Pool configurations. VDI sessions will be redirected to configured "
"gateways instead of the |morpheus| appliance when a VDI Gateway is "
"specified for a VDI Pool."
msgstr ""
"VDI Gateways puede ser linked to a |morpheus| appliance y then used in VDI "
"Pool configurations. VDI sessions será redirected configurard gateways "
"instead of the |morpheus| appliance when a VDI Gateway is specified for a "
"VDI Pool."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:152
msgid ""
"A VDI Gateway is a separate VM or container Instance used to route users "
"to VDI Instances. The |morpheus| VDI Gateway section is for configuring a"
" connection to a VDI Gateway, not creating the gateway Instance itself."
msgstr ""
"A VDI Gateway is a separate VM o container Instance used to route users to "
"VDI Instances. The |morpheus| VDI Gateway section is for configuring a "
"connection to a VDI Gateway, not creating the gateway Instance itself."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:154
msgid ""
"**NAME** Specify a name for the VDI Gateway in |morpheus|. Note that the "
"VDI Gateway Name is not used when connecting to the gateway"
msgstr ""
"**NAME** Specify a name for the VDI Gateway in |morpheus|. Tenga en cuenta "
"que the VDI Gateway Name is no used when connecting to the gateway"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:155
msgid ""
"**DESCRIPTION** Specify a description for the VDI Gateway in |morpheus|. "
"(optional)"
msgstr ""
"**DESCRIPTION** Specify a description for the VDI Gateway in |morpheus|. "
"(optional)"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:156
msgid ""
"**GATEWAY URL** The url of the VDI Gateway. This url is used to connect "
"to the gateway, and should match the the worker url of the VDI Gateway."
msgstr ""
"**GATEWAY URL** The url of the VDI Gateway. This url se utiliza para "
"connect to the gateway, y should match the the worker url of the VDI "
"Gateway."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:158
msgid ""
"Upon creation, the VDI Gateway record will produce an ``API KEY``. This "
"``API KEY`` needs to be specified in the ``morpheus-worker.rb`` file on "
"the API Gateway itself under ``worker['apikey'] = '$API_KEY'``. Once the "
"gateway object is created you will need to configure it as the default "
"gateway in |morpheus| global settings (|AdmSetApp|). Scroll down to the "
"\"Default Console Gateway\" setting and select the gateway object you've "
"just created. Continue on to the next section to actually install the "
"gateway and configure it with your API key."
msgstr ""
"Upon creation, the VDI Gateway record will produce an ``API KEY``. This "
"``API KEY`` necesita ser specified in the ``morpheus-worker.rb`` file on "
"the API Gateway itself under ``worker['apikey'] = '$API_KEY'``. Una vez "
"que el gateway object is created you necesitará configure it as the "
"predeterminado gateway in |morpheus| global settings (|AdmSetApp|). Scroll "
"down to the \"Default Console Gateway\" setting y select the gateway "
"object you've just created. Continue on to the next section to actually "
"install the gateway y configure it con your clave API."

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:161
msgid "VDI Gateway VM Install"
msgstr "VDI Gateway VM Install"

#: ../../tools/vdi_pools.rst:163
